-- title:
--   With generators $a_1,\dots,a_m$ of $\Gamma(Y,W)$, $x\mapsto(a_1(x),\dots,a_m(x))$ embeds $W(\mathbb C)$ in $\mathbb C^m$
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $\sigma:R\to\mathbb C$ a ring homomorphism and $\pi:Y\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ a scheme over $R$. Its **complex points** along $\sigma$ are the morphisms $x:\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb C\to Y$ with $\pi\circ x=\operatorname{Spec}\sigma$, i.e. the $\mathbb C$-points of the base change $Y\times_{R,\sigma}\mathbb C$; they form the space $Y(\mathbb C)$ with the analytic topology of `FiniteFields_BettiNumbers`.
--
--   Let $W\subseteq Y$ be an affine open subscheme, $W(\mathbb C)\subseteq Y(\mathbb C)$ the set of complex points that factor through $W$, and let $a_1,\dots,a_m\in\Gamma(Y,W)$ generate $\Gamma(Y,W)$ as a ring together with the image of $R\to\Gamma(Y,W)$. Then
--   $$W(\mathbb C)\longrightarrow\mathbb C^m,\qquad x\longmapsto\bigl(a_1(x),\dots,a_m(x)\bigr),$$
--   is a topological embedding.
--
--   This identifies the topology of $Y(\mathbb C)$ on an affine open with the classical one: if $\Gamma(Y,W)=R[a_1,\dots,a_m]$, then $W(\mathbb C)$ is homeomorphic to the corresponding subset of $\mathbb C^m$ with the Euclidean topology.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The generating condition is that the subring generated by the $a_j$ and by the image of $R$ (through $\pi^*:\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec}R)\to\Gamma(Y,W)$) is all of $\Gamma(Y,W)$.
-- source:
--   J.-P. Serre, *Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique*, Ann. Inst. Fourier 6 (1956), 1–42, §2, n° 5, Proposition 2 and the following Remarque (pp. 8–9): the topology of the analytic space associated to X is the coarsest one making the regular functions on the Zariski-open subsets of X continuous. Lean: original formalization for this project (Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib 0df444a), file `Bridge/Betti/ComplexPointsAffine.lean`.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FiniteFields_BettiNumbers

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

theorem FiniteFields.Betti.complexPoints_isEmbedding_of_generators {R : Type} [CommRing R] (σ : R →+* ℂ)
    {Y : Scheme.{0}} (π : Y ⟶ Spec (.of R)) (W : Y.Opens) (hW : IsAffineOpen W)
    (m : ℕ) (a : Fin m → Γ(Y, W))
    (ha : Subring.closure (Set.range a ∪
      Set.range fun r : R ↦ π.appLE ⊤ W le_top ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of R)).inv r)) = ⊤) :
    Topology.IsEmbedding (fun x : {x : ComplexPoints σ π // ⊤ ≤ x.1 ⁻¹ᵁ W} ↦
      fun i : Fin m ↦ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of ℂ)).hom (x.1.1.appLE W ⊤ x.2 (a i))) := by sorry
